+### Pre-1.0.0 implementation coherence
+
+Before Harmonia Software `1.0.0`, the solution evolves as one implementation
+of the accepted architecture. When an accepted architectural or software
+contract changes, refactor the affected implementation to conform to the new
+contract. Superseded APIs, implementations and intermediate designs carry no
+backward-compatibility obligation in this period. Affected consumers must
+operate correctly against the accepted current contract.
+
+Use dependency analysis to establish the actual scope. Include the changed
+component, direct and indirect consumers, interfaces and adapters, persistence
+and interchange representations, configuration, integrations, tests and
+fixtures, documentation, and build dependencies where affected. A change is
+complete only when these dependencies have been reconciled and applicable
+regression and integration verification succeeds.
+
+Apply the existing release classification and acceptance rules. At and after
+Harmonia Software `1.0.0`, any compatibility requirements follow the applicable
+release and interface contracts.
+
